    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nSomehow the `v:progpath`'s head is being appended twice to the `vim.env.PATH`. I looked around briefly at the code base and only saw the below where it was happening once.\nhttps://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/e4137a73246f0867c222b15174174a5b4cf36f71/src/nvim/main.c#L1623-L1627\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```shell\nnvim --clean -c '= vim.env.PATH'\n```\nNotice two duplicate paths at the end.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nShould have only one binary head path.\n\n### Discovery\nRunning the below only produces the single path and correct behavior.\n```shell\nnvim --clean -Es -c '_' -c ':put = expand($Path)' -c ':print' \n```\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1095+g53cbf66bd2\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, vim 9.2.838\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nWindows Version 23H2 OS Build 22631.6345\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nwezterm 20240203-110809-5046fc22\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nscoop",
